<title>UK: CRICKET-ENGLISH COUNTY CHAMPIONSHIP SCORES.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-ENGLISH COUNTY CHAMPIONSHIP SCORES.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Scores on the third day of</p>
<p>four-day English county championship matches on Sunday:</p>
<p>At Lord's: Surrey beat Middlesex by an innings and 125 runs.</p>
<p>Middlesex 205 and 201 (J.Pooley 72; Saqlain Mushtaq 5-66),</p>
<p>Surrey 531-9 declared. Surrey 24 points, Middlesex 4.</p>
<p>Hove: Gloucestershire 320 and 271-6 (T.Hancock 84, M.Alleyne</p>
<p>77), Sussex 324 (N.Taylor 74, M.Peirce 73, P.Moores 65; R.Davis</p>
<p>4-35)</p>
<p>Portsmouth: Yorkshire 501-8 declared, Hampshire 281 and</p>
<p>173-3 (J.Laney 81, G.White 58 not out)</p>
<p>Trent Bridge (Nottingham): Somerset 337 and 248-4</p>
<p>(M.Trescothick 70 not out, S.Ecclestone 65), Nottinghamshire 356</p>
<p>(A.Metcalfe 79)</p>
<p>Worcester: Worcestershire 476-9 declared and 263-7 (W.Weston</p>
<p>106 not out), Glamorgan 398 (M.Maynard 161 not out, S.James 69).</p>
</text>
